\xe2\x80\x9cThey (the parents) can see that there is no money in their family but still their child to keep playing football. This hunger does not go until their kid is playing for India at some level,\xe2\x80\x9d he said.

\xe2\x80\x9cFrom childhood, there is a habit instated in children of playing any sport but even they choose football. There are a lot of tournaments as well. A division\xe2\x80\xa6B division\xe2\x80\xa6like that across various age groups including baby leagues,\xe2\x80\x9d he added.

Most recent products of the sublime state are Jeakson Singh and Amarjit Singh Kiyam. The duo was a part of the Indian team in the Under-17 World Cup. Including them, there were eight Manipuri boys in the team that lost 0-4 to Ghana.

Almost half of India\xe2\x80\x99s women\xe2\x80\x99s squad has players from Manipur as well. Shanta points at the unwritten policy adopted by the football clubs where boys and girls in the U15 category have to train together. 

\xe2\x80\x9cAfter a girls team is set, then the coaches make them play with boys after the age of 15. This does not let overconfidence come in. We want the girls to be as good as boys. By this, no one misses on anything and both grow together,\xe2\x80\x9d he said.

Since the culture has revolved around football, any other sport coming in seems impossible. This is somewhat similar to the cricket inclination that India has. \xe2\x80\x9cCricket is not that famous. People don\xe2\x80\x99t even watch it. It\xe2\x80\x99s all about football,\xe2\x80\x9d said Shanta.

\xe2\x80\x9cThere are not too many jobs in Manipur. Most of them aspire to get a job in the police if football does not work,\xe2\x80\x9d he added.

'

