"It may be kept in mind that whenever an Indian citizen acquires foreign nationality he is expected to surrender his Indian passport. India continues to pursue Choksi's return with the government of Antigua through diplomatic and legal channels,'' said a government source.

"The return of passport is more of a formality as he had ceased to be an Indian citizen when he acquired Antigua citizenship last year,'' said another officer.

In August last year, India gave Antigua a request for Choksi's extradition. A team from India was also sent to Antigua to pursue the request. Choksi is wanted in India by CBI and the Enforcement Directorate, which are probing the PNB fraud, one of the biggest banking scams in the country.

Choksi, one of the alleged masterminds of the nearly Rs 14000 crore scam in PNB and a uncle of fugitive diamantaire Nirav Modi, took citizenship of Antigua last year. 


