b'Mumbai: Kotak Mahindra Bank has reported a net profit of Rs 1,291 crore for the quarter ended December 2018 \xe2\x80\x94 23% higher over the net profit of Rs 1,053 crore in the corresponding period in the previous year. Announcing the results on Monday, the bank\xe2\x80\x99s Joint MD Dipak Gupta said that the bank had improved its net interest margin following the scaling down of loans by NBFCs. Advances, as on December 31, 2018, were up 23% to Rs 1.9 lakh crore from Rs 1.6 lakh crore a year earlier. The increase in lending also resulted in the bank\xe2\x80\x99s ratio of gross NPAs improving to 2.07% from 2.31% in the same period a year ago. The overall quantum of NPAs decreased by Rs 125 crore because of a special dispensation by the RBI on asset recognition for MSMEs announced earlier this month.

