b'MUMBAI: The Supreme Court-appointed Committee of Administrators (CoA) are bringing into effect a behavioural counselling programme for cricketers at all age levels, and the process is merely in line with what has been in practice at the National Cricket Academy (NCA) in Bangalore under the watchful eyes of India's junior national coach and former batting legend Rahul Dravid.


