\xe2\x80\x9cVidarbha were averaging 400 runs in the first innings in the last season. We bowled them out for 246, which was a really good effort,\xe2\x80\x9d Whatmore continued, pondering over the lost chances. \xe2\x80\x9cBut certain things occurred, like they do in every game, and we weren\xe2\x80\x99t able to capitalize.\xe2\x80\x9d

Revenge, however, is a dish best served cold. Coach Whatmore is banking on his players to put the adage into practice over the next five days. 

\xe2\x80\x9cWe have learnt from that experience, which was evident in our last match against Gujarat. We hope to keep going, hope to enjoy our cricket, hope to back each other up and play a good game,\xe2\x80\x9d Whatmore said.

It has been a dream season for Kerala so far. They have earned the respect of rivals. 

\xe2\x80\x9cKerala have done well throughout the season. Two good teams would be playing tomorrow,\xe2\x80\x9d Vidarbha coach Chandrakant Pandit said.

Past records apart, the burden of expectation hangs heavy over both camps. Vidarbha, the defending champions, have to prove that their dominance wasn\xe2\x80\x99t a one-off thing. They haven\xe2\x80\x99t faced defeat this season, and fans back home expect them to carry on in the same vein.

\xe2\x80\x9cPressure is always there. When you start your innings, there is pressure. You want to win every game...that creates pressure. You want to maintain your reputation, that thought puts you under pressure. But one should be able to handle that in the middle,\xe2\x80\x9d Pandit said. 

\xe2\x80\x9cOur team had done really well last season. They faced tough situations on the ground. We experienced the pressure last year, when we played the semifinal, and then won the final. So we are used to the pressure,\xe2\x80\x9d Pandit added.

Kerala, on the other hand, have reached the semi-final for the first time. With multiple challenges \xe2\x80\x94 the sense of occasion, playing at home, pressure of continuing with the history-making spree \xe2\x80\x94 Kerala have their plate full. 

Whatmore talked about avoiding these \xe2\x80\x98distractions\xe2\x80\x99.

\xe2\x80\x9cAll the players are happy to get to this stage. We have got to a position where we have been never before, which is very significant. The challenge now is to treat this as just another match, to enjoy the game, to avoid the obvious distractions and to trust each other,\xe2\x80\x9d Whatmore said. 

Whatmore\xe2\x80\x99s advice for Kerala boys, though sound, will be far from easy to heed. It didn\xe2\x80\x99t look that Kerala skipper Sachin Baby was taking this match as \xe2\x80\x98just another game\xe2\x80\x99 when he talked about his aspirations.

\xe2\x80\x9cThe feeling is awesome. When I made my Ranji debut in 2009, my captain was Sreesanth. Since that time, I have been hearing people say that we want Kerala to play the Irani Trophy. For that, you have to win the Ranji Trophy. I used to think that if I make it possible, that will be the biggest achievement of my life,\xe2\x80\x9d Baby said.


'

