b'NEW DELHI: Sarfraz Ahmed runs the risk of being suspended if the match officials of the second One-Day International between Pakistan and South Africa find that the Pakistan skipper breached International Cricket Council\xe2\x80\x99s (ICC) anti-racism code.


Sarfraz, on Tuesday, was heard on stump-mic making what could be perceived as racist comments towards South African all-rounder Andile Phehlukwayo during the second ODI in Durban.


