        \xe2\x80\x9cYou alone don\xe2\x80\x99t control your privacy on social media platforms. Your friends have a say too,\xe2\x80\x9d said Jim Bagrow, a mathematician at the University of Vermont who led the research published in the journal Nature Human Behavior. Tech giants including Google, Facebook and Twitter have come under increased scrutiny over the way they handle users\xe2\x80\x99 personal information to target advertising.


\xe2\x80\x9cThere\xe2\x80\x99s no place to hide in a social network,\xe2\x80\x9d study co-author Lewis Mitchell said. \xe2\x80\x9cInformation is so strongly embedded in a social network that individuals can be profiled from their social ties even when they forgo the platform ,\xe2\x80\x9d researchers said. 

