        The appeal requested the NCLT to direct the resolution professional to drop the categorisation of EPFO (Employees\xe2\x80\x99 PF organisation) dues under Section 53 (1) (f) of the IBC as \xe2\x80\x98other remaining debts and dues\xe2\x80\x99.The Regional PF Commissioner petitioned the NCLT after the official liquidator of Tirunelveli-based Karpagam Spinners, which is under CIRP, rejected the claim for recovery of PF dues. Citing an earlier judgement given by the Supreme Court (SC), member, judicial, NCLT, Chennai, CH. Mohd. Sharief Tariq said that I&B Code, 2016, will override anything inconsistent contained in the EPF and MP (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act, 1952.\xe2\x80\x9cThe application filed by filed by the applicant viz EPFO is devoid of merits and stands rejected,\xe2\x80\x9d he said. \xe2\x80\x9cThe verification and admission of the claim of the applicant has correctly been recorded by the liquidator,\xe2\x80\x9d Tariq ruled.\xe2\x80\x9cNotwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in any law enacted by the Parliament or any State Legislature for the time being in force, the proceeds from the sale of the liquidation assets shall be distributed in the following order of priority and within such period and in such manner as may be specified,\xe2\x80\x9d according to Section 53 of IBC. Under this classification, \xe2\x80\x98other remaining debts and dues\xe2\x80\x99 rank far lower in the list of eligible categories/persons to whom payments have to be made during liquidation. Workmen dues and dues owed to employees (administrative staff) are however ranked higher in the priority list. \xe2\x80\x9cThe claim of the \xe2\x80\x98PF Commissioner\xe2\x80\x99 to statutory first charge cannot be granted in view of Section 53 (of IBC),\xe2\x80\x9d said K S Ravichandran of KSR&Co, Company Secretaries. \xe2\x80\x9cBut contributions to \xe2\x80\x98Provident Fund\xe2\x80\x99 must be treated as workmen dues only. They are supposed to be accorded the same rank as workmen dues,\xe2\x80\x9d he said. \xe2\x80\x9cThe claim (of the PF Commissioner) should not have been classified under \xe2\x80\x98other remaining debts and dues\xe2\x80\x99 that rank far lower in the priority list. The \xe2\x80\x98PF Commissioner\xe2\x80\x99 can claim the dues under Section 53 (b) (for workmen) and (c) (for administrative staff),\xe2\x80\x9d Ravichandran explained. '

