b'NEW DELHI: While the mobile phone and TV markets are witnessing a steady rise in the Indian market, another segment that is going strong is the wearables market. Comprising primarily of smartwatches and fitness bands that cater to a varied set of audiences, the segment, however, is somehow failing to exhibit a sense of innovation with customers. Both smartwatches and fitness bands that we see every year are mere upgrades, which are marketed as major selling points. 

And most of these upgrades are generally visible in cheaper fitness bands, not smartwatches as the former has more room for improvements in addition to several other factors. So, with ever improving fitness bands, is the smartwatch segment in trouble? We got in touch with IDC, Counterpoint and one of the known brands in the wearable market - Honor. Here\xe2\x80\x99s what they think about it.



