The launch is PSLV\xe2\x80\x99s 46th flight and the first flight with a new variant of PSLV called PSLV-DL with two strap-ons, each carrying 12.2-tonne of solid propellent.



PSLV-C44 launch: Here\xe2\x80\x99s why this mission lifted off at midnight\xe2\x80\x9cLaunch time depends on the requirement of the satellite. They wanted the satellite to cross south to north of equator around noon, maybe due to sunlight condition. Our launcher goes from north to south of the equator. To meet the requirement, we needed to have a night launch,\xe2\x80\x9d said K Sivan, Isro chairman. Microsat-R has been designed for military by DRDO.


Around 13 minutes into the mission, the fourth and final stage (PS4) of PSLV injected the primary payload Microsat-R at an altitude of about 277.2km. Microsat R has been developed by Defence Research and Development Organisation (DRDO) laboratories.

PM Modi tweeted a congratulation to the scientists behind the successful launch.


With this launch, India also becomes the first country to use the fourth stage of a space rocket as an orbital plat\xe2\x80\xa6 https://t.co/QkHxs1cL1z\xe2\x80\x94 Narendra Modi (@narendramodi) 1548376586000

Congratulating the team for the successful mission, Isro chairman K Sivan said this was the first that PSLV was \xe2\x80\x9cflown to the lowest orbit.\xe2\x80\x9d

Sivan congratulated the students who designed Kalamsat and said, \xe2\x80\x9cFor the first time the PS4 will be revived for students to do experiments.\xe2\x80\x9d

After the injection of Microsat-R, the PS4 would be reignited and shut off twice, as the stage with an increased velocity is raised to an orbit about 450km in altitude.

An hour and 40 minutes after the launch, the PS4, which would become a rocket debris after its engine is shut off and its fuel depleted, would be revived through solar panels and batteries. Kalamsat, weighing about 1.2kg, still secured to the stage, would be then activated.

PS4 is the smallest of the stages in size with a height of 2.5m and a diameter of 1.34m carrying 1.6 tonne propellent. With two liquid engines applying a thrust of 7.6kN each, PS4 is responsible for the correct injection of the payloads into their respective desired orbits.

According to Isro officials, PS4 will stay \xe2\x80\x98alive\xe2\x80\x99 for the next six months before it drifts away and disintegrates upon reaching the earth\xe2\x80\x99s atmosphere. In the meantime, the cubesat made of space grade aluminium will be tested for its communication module, onboard computer, solar panels and electronics designed and developed by Indian students. The data from the tiny satellite will be collected by ground stations.


