Ridiculed by cricket fans and fraternity for their handling of the enquiry, the CoA did a U-turn on its own recent decisions regarding the matter. The Vinod Rai-led committee sent out a statement on Thursday evening that read: \xe2\x80\x9cSince the adjudication of all allegations of misconduct against any cricketer registered with, inter alia, the BCCI is required to be undertaken by the BCCI Ombudsman, whose appointment is pending directions of the Hon\xe2\x80\x99ble Supreme Court of India, the CoA is the of the view that the interim suspension orders dated 11.01.2019 should be presently lifted with immediate effect\xe2\x80\x9d.

With skipper Virat Kohli being rested for the last two ODIs (and three T20Is), Pandya will technically be the replacement. Vijay Shankar and Shubman Gill, who were earlier sent to New Zealand as replacements for Pandya and Rahul, will continue to be in the team. Rahul, who was part of the earlier announced T20 squad for the three matches in New Zealand, will join the team in the first week of February.

