b'MELBOURNE: Naomi Osaka, the fourth-seeded Japanese, and Czech Petra Kvitova, the two-time major winner, will fight for the Daphne Akhurst Memorial Cup and then some more in the Australian Open final on Saturday. The duo - power hitters and heavy servers -- will also be locked in for a shootout for the No. 1 ranking, a win-one-and take-two affair.


On an oven-hot day at Melbourne Park, the eighth-seeded Kvitova extended her winning streak to 11 matches when she ended the challenge of unseeded American Danielle Collins 7-6 (7-2), 6-0 in the semifinals. Osaka followed up her maiden major title at the US Open by making the final in the opening Grand Slam of the year, beating Serena Williams' conqueror Karolina Pliskova 6-2, 4-6, 6-4.


