b'MUMBAI: A rising debt obligation, combined with crashing stock prices of group companies, forced Zee chief Subhash Chandra to come out in the open on Friday to acknowledge that his empire was facing an uphill task with its finances. He also apologised to lenders that he had not lived up to their expectations. 


With a large number of lenders waiting for Chandra to arrange some funds to meet requirements by Monday, the chance of a further crash in stock prices next week could not be ruled out, brokers and mutual fund managers said.


