b'Chennai: Indian Overseas Bank (IOB) reported a 64.4% year-on-year (y-o-y) fall in net loss to Rs 346.02 crore in Q3 of 2018-19 (FY19) on the back of a strong growth in non-interest income. The bank registered a net loss of Rs 971.2 crore in Q3 of FY18. Total income increased 12.4% y-o-y to Rs 5,689 crore while non-interest income surged 41.8% y-o-y to Rs 1,146 crore during Q3 of FY19.

