The paid-up equity of CESC would remain Rs 132 crore while that of the retail entity would be Rs 40 crore and other ventures was Rs 26 crore. CESC Ventures has the BPO (Firstsource Solutions), IT and Quest. It will have a turnover of Rs 4,500 crore, including Firstsource and profit of Rs 400 crore. 

In all these companies, promoters will have 50% stake each. Spencer\xe2\x80\x99s Retail has the retail business with Rs 2,500crore turnover. CESC had taken an NCLT approval under the Companies Act for the demerger. CESC\xe2\x80\x99s distribution and generation demerger will remain pending until the WBERC\xe2\x80\x99s green nod is available. 

Spencer\xe2\x80\x99s Retail and CESC Ventures will be a part of the trade-for-trade segment for 10 trading days.

