b'MANGALORE: Indian media and entertainment industry is projected to grow at a CAGR of 11.7% from USD 30,364 million in 2017 to USD 52,683 million in 2022 due to rising populations, increasing disposable incomes and new technologies have fuelled the growth of all forms of content consumption, be it cinema, television or over-the-top (OTT) services, according to an ASSOCHAM-PwC joint study.


Television, cinema and OTT will collectively account for 46% of the overall growth in the Indian entertainment and media industry for the period from 2017 to 2022, noted ASSOCHAM-PwC joint study on \xe2\x80\x98Video on Demand: Entertainment reimagined\xe2\x80\x99.


