CBI books Chanda Kochhar, her husband and Venugopal Dhoot for irregularities in six high-value loans


The information provided by CBI also comes in the backdrop of senior minister Arun Jaitley going public with a blog where he expressed concern over a list of top bankers named in the FIR, putting them in the line of investigation. The minister said this amounted to 

  "investigative adventurism"
 + and the agency was better advised to keep its eye on the main targets.

Jaitley comments were seen to be directed at the CBI leadership, rather than investigators lower down the ranks, as it is the agency director who decides on the FIR in important cases. The names of top bankers could not have been included without the nod of senior officers, including interim CBI director M Nageswara Rao.



Among those the CBI sought to probe are Sandeep Bakshi, CEO-MD of ICICI Bank; K V Kamath, chairman of New Development Bank set up by BRICS; Sonjoy Chatterjee, chairman of Goldman Sachs India; K Ramkumar, former executive director of ICICI Bank; N S Kannan, MD & CEO of ICICI Prudential Life; Zarin Daruwala, CEO of Standard Chartered Bank India; Rajiv Sabharwal, MD-CEO of Tata Capital, and Homi Khusrokhan, board member of ICICI Bank.

The CBI accused Mishra, an Indian Revenue Service (IRS) officer, of going slow in the Kochhar probe, saying the preliminary enquiry was registered in December 2017 but the investigation was \xe2\x80\x9cunnecessarily kept pending\xe2\x80\x9d. The high profile case involves allegations that loans were given to Videocon when Kochhar was heading the private bank and there was quid pro quo by way of Rs 64 crore paid by Dhoot to her husband. Deepak Kochhar and Dhoot are accused of setting up businesses which were used to route the money.

The officer was replaced by another SP, Mohit Gupta, who supervised the raids on Videocon offices in Mumbai and Aurangabad and Deepak Kochhar\xe2\x80\x99s companies on January 24.

Interestingly, the CBI refused to issue a formal statement on the matter or even explain why senior officers failed to act for over a year if Mishra was sitting on the probe. At the time of registration of the PE, only Deepak Kochhar and Dhoot were named but in its FIR last week, Chanda Kochhar too was named as an accused, alleging she took illegal gratification in lieu of loans of Rs 1,875 crore to the Videocon group.

\xe2\x80\x9cICICI Bank case was one of the very important cases pending without progress. It was reviewed some time back after which the probe was accelerated and converted into a regular case (FIR) on January 22,\xe2\x80\x9d a CBI official said. Mishra signed the FIR as main SP of the agency\xe2\x80\x99s Bank Securities and Fraud Cell (BS&FC).

The CBI on Sunday said after registration of the FIR, searches were proposed to be conducted. \xe2\x80\x9cHowever, it was suspected that there was a possibility of information regarding searches being leaked. A discreet inquiry was conducted and role of Sudhanshu Dhar Mishra was strongly suspected. Hence, he has been transferred pending detailed inquiry in the matter,\xe2\x80\x9d an officer said. The agency added that role of \xe2\x80\x9cothers\xe2\x80\x9d along with Mishra were also being probed for keeping the PE pending.

The agency also couldn\xe2\x80\x99t explain that if Mishra was delaying the probe and leaking raid information, why was he allowed to file the FIR under his name on January 22. Mishra couldn\xe2\x80\x99t be reached for his comments.

Usually, in important and sensitive cases like the one against Kochhar, a decision to register an FIR is taken at various levels including the SP, DIG, joint director and additional director with the director having the final say. In the ICICI Bank case, the supervising joint director, Praveen Sinha, too was moved out of BS&FC and joint director V Murugesan was given the charge.

Interim CBI director Rao has made several transfers in the past three weeks. Around 30 officers including joint directors, DIGs, SPs and additional SPs have been moved to different branches, which according to the agency, is part of a \xe2\x80\x9ccleansing\xe2\x80\x9d exercise.

'

