b'NEW DELHI: Going beyond political rhetoric about electronic voting machines, Congress has asked its state units to carry out \xe2\x80\x9cintensive training\xe2\x80\x9d of leaders to be deputed for Election Commission-mandated checking of EVMs in the run-up to elections.


According to an AICC directive to Congress state presidents, they should focus on checking of EVMs that the EC allows to political parties in four stages, the first being well ahead of voting and the last being an hour before polling.


