b'MUMBAI: Marriott International, the world\xe2\x80\x99s largest lodging company, is considering buying a significant minority stake in Chandru L Raheja\xe2\x80\x99s hotels business, according to people familiar with the matter. Marriott plans to acquire at least 10% in Chalet Hotels, which owns high-end properties in India \xe2\x80\x94 including the JW Marriott Mumbai and the Bengaluru Marriott \xe2\x80\x94 for about Rs 574 crore. Besides Chalet Hotels, Raheja owns Shoppers Stop, in which Jeff Bezos\xe2\x80\x99s Amazon has an investment, and Inorbit Mall.

Typically, international lodging companies don\xe2\x80\x99t invest in properties as they prefer to be asset-light while focusing on franchising their brands and managing hotels. But, they do loosen their purse strings to invest in select properties.



