b'CHANDIGARH/JIND: Officials of State Bank of India (SBI) have alleged that data of the Unique Identification Authority of India (UIDAI) has been misused. Logins and biometrics of their Aadhaar operators have been misused to generate unauthorised Aadhaar cards, bank officials informed UIDAI. Countering the charge, UIDAI said, \xe2\x80\x9cAadhaar database is fully secured and no security breach, biometric or otherwise, has taken place.\xe2\x80\x9d


SBI, like other banks, was given an Aadhaar enrolment target for which it selected vendors \xe2\x80\x94 FIA Technology Services Pvt Ltd and Sanjivini Consultants Pvt Ltd \xe2\x80\x94 in the Chandigarh region which covers Haryana, Punjab, Himachal, J&K and the UT of Chandigarh itself. However, of close to 250 operators employed with these agencies, nearly half were penalised in the last two months and were either deactivated or blacklisted. This brought SBI\xe2\x80\x99s Aadhaar enrolments to a halt at many branches, causing the bank to fail to meet targets and face penalties.


