b'Mumbai: Over 90% of electricity utilities and almost all telecom providers and direct-to-home (DTH) broadcasters are plugged into the Bharat Bill Payment System (BBPS). This makes the anywhere-anytime facility available to a large section of the population.

BBPS is a centralised bill payment system under the National Payments Corporation of India (NPCI), which gathers details of bills issued by electricity, water, telephone, DTH and gas utilities instantly across the country. Speaking to TOI, BBPS chief project officer A R Ramesh said that, among the current category of billers, several water utilities are yet to join.



