b'Chennai: Renault-Nissan Alliance India has signed a memorandum of understanding with National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC) to train its workforce in the alliance plant in Oragadam for future technologies. The first year of partnership aims to get 10% of employees trained to be able to support the growth and expansion plans of Renault-Nissan Alliance in India. Through this partnership, NSDC will assist the Renault-Nissan workforce develop competency standards in emerging automotive manufacturing technologies. Also Renault-Nissan Alliance will customise an engagement and \xe2\x80\x9cskilling action plan along with NSDC\xe2\x80\x99s network for program design, development and employment sustainability from the demand side,\xe2\x80\x9d said the company in a statement. Renault-Nissan Alliance will provide support through onsite labs, training, mentorship, internship and / or participation of expert domains. It will also mobilise Renault-Nissan Alliance workforce and encourage upskilling and reskilling through dual TVET and apprenticeship. It will also lead and conduct seminars, workshops, technical task forces etc. to identify and propagate industry relevant technology, knowledge and skill to support the National Skill Development Mission.

