        Out of 898 ongoing processes, 275 cases have passed 270 days since admission while another 166 cases have crossed 180 days since admission. So far, out of 1,484 cases admitted under the insolvency process, only 79 have seen approval of resolution plans, and even among those, repayments are yet to be made to lenders. \xe2\x80\x9cCorporate debtors are using all legal avenues including appeals in the Supreme Court. So, the process is getting delayed,\xe2\x80\x9d explained K S Ravichandran of KSR&Co, Company Secretaries. 

Essar Steel, which is one of the biggest defaulters, is a case in point.

The owners of Essar Steel, which owes nearly Rs 51000 crore to banks, have challenged the bankruptcy court\xe2\x80\x99s decision to sell the steel producer to Arcelor Mittal in the Supreme Court. The nine months (270 days) set for the process has now stretched beyond 1 \xc2\xbd years.

\xe2\x80\x9cThe law is evolving and a lot of amendments have been made (to the IBC). So, it took time for resolution professionals and committee of creditors to understand the implication of these amendments,\xe2\x80\x9d a senior insolvency resolution professional (RP) said. New cases admitted under CIRP in Q3 of FY19 accounted for 18% of all cases admitted so far. Out of the total admitted cases (1484) till Q3, about 50% (744 cases) were admitted in the first nine months of FY19. \xe2\x80\x9cIBC is a convenient tool for creditors to get their dues within a stipulated timeframe. So, they are using it in a big way to recover money,\xe2\x80\x9d Ravichandran said. 

\xe2\x80\x9cUnder such circumstances, the number of cases facing liquidation will see a significant increase in the next few quarters,\xe2\x80\x9d observers tracking resolution processes said. Incidentally, out of the 134 cases which were closed in Q3 of FY19, only 13 cases were resolved while 78 cases faced liquidation. In all, 52% of all closed cases (586) till Q3 were through liquidation while only 34 (13%) cases were resolved with an average haircut of about 52% on admitted claims.


