b'Mumbai: Pledged shares are suddenly an anathema to Dalal Street traders. On Friday, Zee Group shares had crashed due to offloading of nearly 65 lakh pledged shares in flagship Zee Entertainment. In the next session on Monday, it was the turn of large companies in which substantial chunks of promoters\xe2\x80\x99 shares are pledged to witness a sharp slide in their stocks. Sterlite Technology, in which nearly 97% of the promoters\xe2\x80\x99 holding has been pledged with lenders, tanked over 7%. Reliance Infrastructure, which has nearly 84% of the promoters\xe2\x80\x99 shares pledged, lost 5% on the exchange. 

On Friday, several mutual funds were hit after some lenders sold about 65 lakh shares of Zee Entertainment, which crashed 26%. Another 2.4 crore shares of the other group company Dish TV were sold by IIFL and Edelweiss arms, pulling the stock down by nearly 33%. 



