A report by Edelweiss in October 2018 had mentioned that the cascading impact of sharp slides in stock prices and subsequently on pledged holdings by promoters tends to be quite severe. \xe2\x80\x9cCompanies where pledges are high and market sentiments have dragged the share prices down are bound to witness higher volatility,\xe2\x80\x9d the report had said. In terms of value, pledged holding stood at Rs 2.1 lakh crore at the end of September 2018, down marginally from Rs 2.4 lakh as of June 2018. 

The latest figures for pledged shares is yet to be compiled. 

The Edelweiss report had mentioned that stocks like Dish TV, Reliance Capital, Centrum Capital, Adani Ports and Just Dial had seen consistent incremental pledging activity in the last five quarters. Stocks like Future Enterprises, Bajaj Corporation, Fortis Healthcare and Sterlite Technologies had seen a sharp jump in promoter pledging activity during the July-September quarter. \xe2\x80\x9cIn tumultuous times like these, trends in promoter pledging information becomes quite crucial for the investors as it provides cues on potential volatility in a stock,\xe2\x80\x9d the report had mentioned.

Along with NBFCs, mutual funds are also active in providing money to promoters against pledged shares. Although fund houses insist everything is above board, after Friday\xe2\x80\x99s sharp slide in Zee Entertainment and MFs\xe2\x80\x99 exposure in the stock, market players have been questioning if everything is according to the rules. 

\xe2\x80\x9cIt was only three months ago that NBFCs and mutual funds were rapped on the knuckles for misuse of commercial papers (in the IL&FS case). The market is now surprised that so soon they seem to be violating all norms of LAS (loan against shares),\xe2\x80\x9d said Arun Kejriwal, director of investment advisory firm KRIS. \xe2\x80\x9cOne wonders if investors should be investing in debt funds at all,\xe2\x80\x9d he added.

Last week, the Sun Pharma stock was hit on news that the promoters had pledged shares to invest in a real estate company that was linked to the drug major\xe2\x80\x99s main promoter.


'

