b'Mumbai: Tata Steel will sell 70% stake in its Southeast Asian operations to China\xe2\x80\x99s HBIS Group for $327 million (Rs 2,325 crore) as it looks to reduce exposure to overseas markets and ramp up its presence at home through acquisitions. The move comes after the company restructured its European operations by creating a joint venture with Thyssenkrupp, which is under the scrutiny of the regulator there.

