Sources said BJP chief Amit Shah has asked Union HRD minister Prakash Javdekar to begin alliance talks with the Sena. But how to delicately clear decks for an alliance with BJP after years of mudslinging and to convince the Sena rank and file about the need for a tie-up is a challenge for Uddhav, sources said. \xe2\x80\x9cAgrarian unrest, anti-incumbency and the Congress-NCP alliance may pose a threat to the saffron alliance. It is good for BJP and Sena to stay together,\xe2\x80\x9d a BJP leader said. A Sena MP noted that \xe2\x80\x9cneither Sena nor BJP can afford a division of Hindutva votes.\xe2\x80\x9d While LS polls are due in the first half of the year, the state elections are due in October. Also, BJP\xe2\x80\x99s ex-ally Raju Shetti is likely to join the opposition alliance.

'

b'NEW DELHI: The government on Monday asked state-run lenders to make overdraft facility and accident insurance for Jan Dhan accounts more attractive, even as banks promised to step up lending under the PM Awas Yojana and to small businesses.


The government\xe2\x80\x99s thrust on some of the segments such as Jan Dhan and MSMEs are seen to be part of a series of sops for voters in the run up to the general elections. Banks are currently allowed to offer Rs 5,000 overdraft under the PM Jan Dhan Yojana if certain basic criteria are met. Many fear the facility will result in a pile-up of bad debt, something that the government has denied.


