b'PUNE: Prime Minister Narendra Modi\xe2\x80\x99s Pariksha Pe Charcha (Discussion on Exams) has garnered the much-needed attention in the state and now the Maharashtra State Council of Educational Research and Training (MSCERT) has issued a mandate to all government-run schools to screen the discussion for students.


MSCERT has also asked schools to send a report of the same to the Zilla Parishad. But the plight of schools in rural areas seems to be overlooked as many teachers are under pressure to arrange the basic infrastructure needed to screen such programmes.


