 With Kia Motors commencing operations, Andhra Pradesh is hopeful of transforming Anantapuramu from one of the most backward regions in the country to an investment hotspot, Andhra Pradesh CM N Chandrababu Naidu said here on Tuesday while inaugurating the Kia Motors plant.

He said the region is geared up to attract more investments, especially in the automotive sector and generate employment for the local population.

Inaugurating Kia Motors plant here, he said the government was able to convince Kia to set up its plant in the drought prone region after it had provided water supply. 

Apart from housing the latest technologies, the Kia Motors plant also houses a five-acre training facility that offers a Basic Technical Course (BTC) in automobiles in collaboration with the Andhra Pradesh State Skill Development Corporation (APSSDC) to help develop manufacturing skills among youth.


