b'AHMEDABAD/MUMBAI: The Ruia family\xe2\x80\x99s attempt to regain control of their flagship Essar Steel by proposing a Rs 54,389-crore offer to settle all debts of the beleaguered company has been rejected by a court.


The Ahmedabad-bench of the National Company Law Tribunal (NCLT) said that financial creditors are not wrong in rejecting the promoters\xe2\x80\x99 settlement plan. The lenders, which had approved ArcelorMittal\xe2\x80\x99s Rs 42,202-crore offer, had said that they will consider Ruias\xe2\x80\x99 settlement plan only if they are directed to do so by the court. 


