The tribunal said that only an applicant who has initiated insolvency against a company can withdraw from the process, and hence the promoters\xe2\x80\x99 settlement proposal is not maintainable. In Essar Steel\xe2\x80\x99s case, SBI and Standard Chartered Bank had filed the insolvency petitions against the company.

The development diminishes the chances for the billionaire Ruia brothers to keep the steelmaker under their fold. The tribunal\xe2\x80\x99s ruling comes amid differing views from industrialists on Ruias\xe2\x80\x99 offer for Essar Steel. Sajjan Jindal of JSW said that the Ruias should be given a chance to regain control of Essar Steel, while Aditya Mittal of ArcelorMittal said that the offer violated the insolvency rules. Industry speculates that the Ruias have the backing of Jindal to retain control of Essar Steel.

With the tribunal ruling going against them, the Ruias will now approach the higher forum, the National Company Law Appellate Tribunal (NCLAT). Tuesday\xe2\x80\x99s verdict comes after the NCLAT\xe2\x80\x99s recent directive to the lower tribunal to pass an order on the Ruias\xe2\x80\x99 offer. Despite the NCLT rejection, the Ruias maintained that their offer is more compelling than that of ArcelorMittal\xe2\x80\x99s. \xe2\x80\x9cIt seeks to repay all classes of creditors and fulfils the bankruptcy code\xe2\x80\x99s overriding objective of value maximisation that has been established time and again by courts at all levels. We submitted the proposal under the recently introduced Section 12A of the code and the recent judgement of the Supreme Court has established that the section\xe2\x80\x99s provisions are applicable retrospectively,\xe2\x80\x9d an Essar Group spokesperson said. \xe2\x80\x9cWe are awaiting a copy of the full NCLT order and will take a call on next steps after we have thoroughly gone through the contents.\xe2\x80\x9d

ArcelorMittal welcomed the NCLT decision, saying it \xe2\x80\x9cprotects the integrity of the code and ensures its legitimacy as a rules-based law\xe2\x80\x9d. It further said, \xe2\x80\x9cWe hope now for a swift resolution to this case.\xe2\x80\x9d The NCLT will hear the resolution plan submitted by ArcelorMittal on January 30.

