b'CHENNAI: Want to stream your favourite show without disruptions? Do it between 4am and 5am, for that when data speeds are maximum, almost 5 times faster than what it is at 10 in the night, a report said.


A research report by OpenSignal showed that smartphone users in the 20 Indian cities analysed experienced fastest download speeds of 16.8 Mbps at 4 am, compared to slowest speed of 3.7 mbps at 10 pm, and daily average speed of 6.5 mbps. A 2-hour movie is about 2 gigabytes of data, and with 4 mbps service it would take about an hour and 15 minutes to download. Where you live also determines your internet speeds, notes the study, which found that Navi Mumbai scored 8.1 Mbps in average LTE download speed, while Prayagraj (Allahabad) came last with almost half the speed at an average 4.0 Mbps speed.


