Government officials said completely built EVs will continue to attract 25% import duty, while those with petrol- and diesel-fired engines face up to 100% levy.

The move on EVs follows a decision by the Prime Minister\xe2\x80\x99s Office to encourage these vehicles to address the growing emission problems in the country with cities such as Delhi grappling with a perpetual problem of haze. The import duty changes are seen to be part of a wider policy push (to be unveiled next month) to provide subsidy for purchase of electric vehicles, especially two-and threewheelers and buses used in public transport.

