The organisers, Rajasthan Cycling Association, a newly-formed body, expressed their helplessness. \xe2\x80\x9cThis is all that we have,\xe2\x80\x9d the officials said. 

True, there have been financial constraints for them. The officials had to dip into their personal reserves to meet the almost Rs 75 lakh budget, which includes renovation of the velodrome that has rarely been used in its two decades of existence. The Cycling Federation of India has given them Rs 5 lakh and has assured another five. State sports minister Ashok Chandna has granted the same amount and assured another Rs 10 lakh from the chief minister\xe2\x80\x99s fund.

It is not just the hosts. Most of the other teams have been put in similar halls. The Maharastra men\xe2\x80\x99s team have a smaller hall as there are only 22 of them. 

