Some days back, researchers at cybersecurity solution provider Check Point Software Technologies Ltd. shared details of vulnerabilities that could have affected any player of Fortnite.

If exploited, the vulnerability would have given an attacker full access to a user\xe2\x80\x99s account and their personal information as well as enabling them to purchase virtual in-game currency using the victim\xe2\x80\x99s payment card details. The vulnerability would also have allowed for a massive invasion of privacy as an attacker could listen to in-game chatter as well as surrounding sounds and conversations within the victim\xe2\x80\x99s home or other location of play.

