        In the paper, Sebi said that at the time of initial or follow-on offering, the minimum application and allotment lot shall be of 100 units and the value of one such lot shall be within the Rs 15,000-20,000 range. After initial listing, a trading lot should also be of 100 units, it said. Currently, in REITs, the minimum subscription value during the initial or follow-on offer should not be less than Rs 2 lakh, while for InvITs the corresponding amount is Rs 10 lakh. During the post-listing trading, minimum trading value for REITs is Rs 1 lakh while for InvITs it is Rs 5 lakh.

The consultation paper also said that the leverage limit for InvITs should be increased from existing 49% to 70%, but the rider is that the higher limit could be used only for acquiring new infrastructure assets.


