According to Gupta, although the three banks have exited PCA, the question remains whether negative return on asset continues to remain a PCA criteria? Following the RBI announcement, finance secretary Rajeev Kumar said in a tweet that this was an outcome of the government\xe2\x80\x99s \xe2\x80\x984R\xe2\x80\x99 strategy \xe2\x80\x94 recognition of stressed loans as default, recapitalisation of banks, resolution of bad loans, and reform of public sector. \xe2\x80\x9cBanks need to be more responsible, adopt high underwriting and risk management standards to avoid recurrence,\xe2\x80\x9d Kumar added.

The RBI\xe2\x80\x99s move comes two days after a review meeting of banks with interim finance minister Piyush Goyal. In the meeting, Goyal informed banks that if they maintained the trend of improvement in performance, they would exit the PCA soon.

