         Although Maruti Swift continues to be the favourite used car brand since 2016, Bajaj Pulsar has been dethroned after 3 years by Hero Splendor Plus in 2018. 

In luxury cars, Audi A4 which ruled in 2015. 2016 and 2017, has now been dethroned by BMW 5 Series. In super bikes Harley Davidson Street 750 continues on top for second year in a row firmly keeping away earlier favourites KTM Duke and KTM RC.

The rising price arc in used vehicles is a reflection of a similar trend in new vehicles though the curve is sharper. 

\xe2\x80\x9cEvery 7-8 years, the mean price of a passenger vehicle changes by Rs 60,000-Rs 80,000 as the hunger for features increases. Even in entry level people are looking for the higher end variants. Features like AC, power steering, power windows, are now basic features and this also affects the price curve,\xe2\x80\x9d said Mayank Pareek, president-PVBU-Tata Motors.

Interestingly, the study which focusses on Droom\xe2\x80\x99s online platform, saw a greater preference for diesel fuel cars at 59% compared to 39% for petrol cars considering the price disparities experienced throughout the year for petrol, said Sandeep Aggarwal, founder and CEO, Droom.

 \xe2\x80\x9cAlso 34% customers preferred vehicles from Indian manufacturers followed by 21% Japanese and 17% South Korean vehicle manufacturers in CY 2018, showing a steady divergence from obsession with foreign cars,\xe2\x80\x9d he said. 

