The Times of India will run Union Budget 2019 live blog, live updates and live streaming on its official website - 
www.timesofindia.indiatimes.com. 

Along with the Union Budget, the finance minister will also present Railway Budget 2019. Earlier, rail budgets and general budgets were presented separately. However, the govt had scrapped this 92-year-old practice and merged Rail Budget with Union Budget. 

