b'Mumbai: Amitabh Chaudhry, the new CEO of Axis Bank, has impressed markets with his strategy to stress on conservatism, profitability and sustainability even while pursuing growth. The bank, which has posted a turnaround in its third quarter results, has gained Rs 17,000 crore in market cap in a month. In an interview with TOI, Chaudhry speaks of how his stints in Infosys and HDFC have taught him the importance of strengthening the brand. Excerpts:

How much time will it take for the bank\xe2\x80\x99s performance ratios to get back to your long-term trend level?



                (function(){
                  var adContainer = '<div id="div-gpt-ad-1485328452682222244" data-size="fluid" data-adsslot="TOI/TOI_ROS/TOI_ROS_AS/TOI_ROS_AS_Mrec_MID_300" class="webonly alC"></div>';
