b'India\xe2\x80\x99s second-home market has been quite hot for some time, with some buyers seeking to get away from the crowded city and the stresses of work with a vacation home while others view it as a good real estate investment. However, the negative was that even if the property was empty, one had to fork out tax on notional rent.


No longer. The interim Budget has given relief to second home-owners by exempting the second property from tax on notional rent. Currently, if a taxpayer owns more than one house property, one property at the taxpayer\xe2\x80\x99s choice is treated as self-occupied and the other is considered as \xe2\x80\x98deemed to be let out\xe2\x80\x99. This is taxed at market rental value even if the taxpayer does not earn any income from it.


