\xe2\x80\x9cConsidering the difficulty of the middle class having to maintain families at two locations on account of their job, children\xe2\x80\x99s education, care of parents, etc., I am proposing to exempt levy of income tax on notional rent on a second self-occupied house,\xe2\x80\x9d interim Finance Minister Piyush Goyal announced on Friday.

Industry trackers believe the move of exempting tax on notional rent on the second house property will help increase demand for affordable and mid-income housing segment as taxpayers will be encouraged to invest in a second home.

\xe2\x80\x9cWith improved liquidity, demand across the affordable and mid-income housing segment will rise,\xe2\x80\x9d Ramesh Nair, CEO and Country Head, JLL India, said. However, the maximum deduction for interest on housing loans shall continue to remain capped, in the aggregate, at Rs 2 lakh.

While the FM in his speech alluded to the difficulties faced by those who are forced to maintain families at two locations, given the specific provisions of the I-T Act, it appears that no tax on notional rent will be payable if the second house is overseas.

There is one downside. \xe2\x80\x9cTaxpayers who had housing loans on their second property were earlier able to claim deduction for full interest on housing loan, against the notional rental income, which could result in a loss. This loss could be set off against rental income from other properties without any limit or could be carried forward for eight years. Now such set-off is limited to Rs 2 lakh,\xe2\x80\x9d says Puneet Gupta, director, People Advisory Services at EY India.

