b'Often, and especially as families grow, a residential house is sold and two flats are bought in a distant suburb. Or parents dispose of a house and buy apartments for their children. Finance minister Piyush Goyal, who hails from Mumbai \xe2\x80\x93 where real estate is among the costliest in India \xe2\x80\x93 has well understood this practical problem of taxpayers.


The first budget of the BJP-led government in 2014 had restricted the income tax benefit available under section 54 of the Income-Tax Act. Accordingly, a deduction from long term capital gains (LTCGs) on the sale of a residential house would be available only if the same was invested in one residential house in India.


