b'Hyderabad: In a country where over 91% of the listed companies are family controlled, Frank Stangenberg-Haverkamp, chairman of the executive board and family board at E Merck KG, that holds the reins of the world\xe2\x80\x99s oldest pharma company, Darmstadt-headquartered Merck KGaA, feels that business families in India need to draw up a family contract and strengthen the value system within the family as well as organisation to ensure continuity.

\xe2\x80\x9cDraw up a family contract, get some values in the business and ask everyone to follow those values. Third, get outside management because no family has enough talented family members to run the business and once you get the outside management, empower them,\xe2\x80\x9d Stangenberg-Haverkamp, who belongs to the 11th generation of the Merck family, said. He was in the city this weekend to participate in the 7th Asian Conference on Family Business, on the theme \xe2\x80\x98Generations to Generations: Building Family Business Legacy Harmoniously\xe2\x80\x99



