Merck, founded in 1668 at Darmstadt, Germany, by Friedrich Jacob Merck, is one of the oldest family controlled businesses in the world with nearly 350 years of existence. The Merck family currently holds 100% in E Merck KG, a holding company, that in turn holds about 70% of the total capital of the Merck KGaA (the rest 30% is held by public shareholders). E Merck KG does not participate in the management of the company but it makes the fundamental entrepreneurial decisions of the Merck Group. The company employs 51,000 employees in 66 countries and is listed on DAX, the German blue chip stock market index.

