b'NEW DELHI: On Friday, the Sports Authority of India (SAI) announced on its official Twitter handle that Australia\xe2\x80\x99s Brett Clarke has been appointed as chief coach for the junior table tennis team, and China\xe2\x80\x99s Yin Wei as coach for the upcoming Coal India-SAI national TT academy in Kolkata. However, both the veteran coaches have refused to come, citing long delay in their appointment. In fact, the two have found jobs with the federations of some other countries, informed Table Tennis Federation of India (TTFI) secretary general, MP Singh.


According to Singh, both Clarke and Wei informed about their decision to the TTFI through separate mails on Friday evening, the same day when SAI broke the news about their appointment.


