The jibes were initially seen as a reflection of the reservations expressed by the AIADMK\xe2\x80\x99s rank and file against any truck with the BJP. Also, there have been reports that the BJP may go for a post-poll tie-up with the DMK. \xe2\x80\x9cWhat good have they (BJP) done so far? Cyclone Gaja relief funds have not yet come, and there are hundreds of crores pending to be released to TN under GST, and several departments await statutory dues. Imposition of Neet affected the students in Tamil Nadu. In Mekedatu, the Centre has been playing double game \xe2\x80\x93 giving go ahead for the study and taking a contrary stand in the Supreme Court,\xe2\x80\x9d Thambi Durai said.

Analysts feel his opposition to the BJP \xe2\x80\x93 at a time when other leaders are going soft on the Saffron party - stems from the fear that he could lose minority votes, especially in Aravakurichi assembly segment, falling under his Karur LS constituency. But after the presentation of the Union budget, there is a general feeling in the party that the BJP may not fare as badly as was expected earlier. Hence, rejecting a pre-poll tie-up may not be a good idea, said a senior AIADMK leader.

Party sources said senior ministers P Thangamani and S P Velumani visited Delhi at the behest of the BJP high command for electoral talks on Wednesday. Significantly, Palaniswami on Friday commended the interim Union budget as \xe2\x80\x9coverall good\xe2\x80\x9d even as the budget lacked any reference to his repeated requests, including relief for Gaja victims. Minister D Jayakumar, however, sought to clarify that in a party like the AIADMK, difference of opinion was bound to be there. He said they would be sorted out when a final decision is taken. \xe2\x80\x9cWe have availed funds from the Centre, but we don\xe2\x80\x99t agree with the Centre on issues like Mekedatu,\xe2\x80\x9d he said, and went onto hail the sops for farmers, poor, unemployed youth and MSME units in the Union budget.


'

b'CHENNAI: It was a rollercoaster 2018 for R Ashwin. While the off-spinner took 38 wickets from 10 Tests, a spate of injuries in crucial games stalled his progress. A groin injury ahead of the fourth Test in England took a toll at a crucial stage of the game, and an abdominal strain before the second Test in Australia ruled him out for the rest of the series. 


But the 32-year-old is back to playing competitive cricket, turning out for his club MRC (A) in TNCA first division. He bowled 38 overs to pick up four wickets in the first game and scored 51 on Saturday in the second. 


