\xe2\x80\x9cIt\xe2\x80\x99s unfortunate that I sustained back-to-back injuries when I was bowling really well on overseas tours. It\xe2\x80\x99s frustrating but you have to move forward. Now, I am almost back to being 100 per cent fit. I haven\xe2\x80\x99t played back-to-back games for a while. So it\xe2\x80\x99s crucial for me to go through the grind. Now that I am playing in only one format, it is important for me to get some game time and also train,\xe2\x80\x9d Ashwin told reporters here on Saturday.

The last few years had also witnessed Ashwin improvising on his bowling action and trying to develop new weapons before he seemed to settle down into a consistent action during the West Indies series last year. Ashwin said that it is crucial to strike a balance at this stage of his career. 

\xe2\x80\x9cIn terms of action, I want to get the best result as much as possible. But now I want to put lesser load on my body because it\xe2\x80\x99s not easy to come back from an abductor injury and abdomen tear. I need to understand what amount of effort and what sort of loading will suit me. 

"Wrist positions are the culmination of you putting more body into the balls. So I need to know how much side-on I can go, how much of hyper-extension I can give\xe2\x80\xa6 So I need to balance everything out. That\xe2\x80\x99s why I have to train smartly if I have to play a fair amount of games and bowl a number of overs,\xe2\x80\x9d said Ashwin.

Even though Ashwin had last featured in ODIs and T20Is back in 2017, he says he will be prepared if an opportunity comes his way, especially with the World Cup around the corner. In a bid to stay injury-free, he is also aiming to manage his workload. 

\xe2\x80\x9cInjuries aren\xe2\x80\x99t anything which you can hold against a particular player. I do my best in preparation. Whenever I had undergone a fitness test or Yo Yo test, I have always been at the top of the list. But in certain games, my body probably wasn\xe2\x80\x99t listening to me. It probably didn\xe2\x80\x99t have a voice to communicate with me. I didn\xe2\x80\x99t know when to step up the gas and when to pull the gas back. 

"The injury had come and I had to deal with it in a certain way. My ultimate goal now is to play games back to back. To an extent it is also about workload management,\xe2\x80\x9d Ashwin said.

'

b'KOLKATA: Italy overcame a blip on Saturday morning to conquer India 3-1 and march into the Davis Cup Finals. Down for the count after the opening day itself, the home team salvaged pride courtesy Rohan Bopanna and Divij Sharan\xe2\x80\x99s come-from-behind victory over Simone Bolleli and Matteo Berrettini. 


The Indian pair\xe2\x80\x99s 4-6, 6-3, 6-4 triumph had the capacity crowd at South Club baying for more. But Prajnesh Gunneswaran once again cut a sorry figure to surrender 1-6, 4-6 to Andreas Seppi.


