The other selectors are ex-India left-arm spinner Nilesh Kulkarni, Sunil More and Ravi Thakkar. 

Yazdegardi had pushed for the same move last year when the selectors had announced the pre-season probables, but his request was turned down by the Committee of Administrators (CoA) running the MCA. Any such move will require three-fourth majority of the members in the SGM.

\xe2\x80\x9cI\xe2\x80\x99m moving a motion for the SGM by Monday or Tuesday. According to the rule, I\xe2\x80\x99ll have to call for an eight-day notice to the members. I didn\xe2\x80\x99t do it before because the CoA told me that if I call for an SGM, it will be null and void, which was wrong on their part. After they went out, I wrote to the ad-hoc committee. They\xe2\x80\x99ve given me the permission to hold the SGM,\xe2\x80\x9d Yazdegardi told TOI.

On January 28, Yazdegardi had submitted a letter to the MCA CEO CS Nayak to call for an SGM within two days, in this regard, but he was told by the association that the ad-hoc committee currently running the MCA can\xe2\x80\x99t call for such a meeting, though he could do it on his own.

