b'KOLKATA: Amid the standoff between the CBI and Kolkata Police, questions were raised regarding any possible transgression of jurisdiction of the agencies.


CBI joint director (east) Pankaj Kumar Srivastava on Sunday said that the team had gone to police commissioner Rajeev Kumar\xe2\x80\x99s residence to ask him questions. He claimed that \xe2\x80\x9csome of the evidences were missing\xe2\x80\x9d and \xe2\x80\x9cthe agency wanted to record statements of some of the police officers\xe2\x80\x9d. He also alleged that the investigation was being interfered. The CBI officials on Sunday claimed that they had necessary papers in place when they went to Kumar\xe2\x80\x99s residence on Loudon Street.


