Sources in the CBI on Sunday indicated that the agency worked within the legal parameters and never transgressed them. Sources also cited Section 165 of the Code of Criminal Procedure to claim that they can even go for a search without a warrant. This section says that \xe2\x80\x9cwhenever an officer in charge of a police station or a police officer making an investigation\xe2\x80\x9d has \xe2\x80\x9creasonable grounds for believing\xe2\x80\x9d that anything required for the investigation into any offence may be found in a place within the \xe2\x80\x9climits of his police station\xe2\x80\x9d, the officer can go for a search after \xe2\x80\x9crecording in writing the grounds of his belief\xe2\x80\x9d. The CBI sources also said that in case of serving summons, the agency\xe2\x80\x99s officers do not need any permission from the police.

Srivastava on Sunday said that they had earlier moved the Supreme Court in 2017 and the apex court in 2018 had ordered that the agency (police) should cooperate. Accordingly, the officials reached the police commissioner\xe2\x80\x99s residence on Sunday.

Kolkata Police sources on Sunday said that the CBI officials were stopped and asked if they had any document necessary for their action. When the officials showed some documents, they wanted to verify contents of those papers. \xe2\x80\x9cHence, they were taken to the Shakespeare Sarani police station. No jurisdiction was crossed in the process,\xe2\x80\x9d a Kolkata Police officer claimed.

The CBI officials have further indicated that Section 41 of the CrPC has empowered them to make arrests even without warrant. The section of the act mentions that \xe2\x80\x9cany police officer without an order from the magistrate and without a warrant can arrest any person\xe2\x80\x9d if the person has been \xe2\x80\x9cconcerned in any cognizable offence\xe2\x80\x9d or against whom \xe2\x80\x9creasonable complaint has been made\xe2\x80\x9d. If the agency has \xe2\x80\x9ca reasonable suspicion\xe2\x80\x9d he can be arrested without a warrant.

Sources said that CRPF were sent to man the CBI offices in Nizam Palace and the CGO Complex and the residence of the joint director (east) of the central agency. Srivastava reasoned that the CRPF came to ensure \xe2\x80\x9csafety and security\xe2\x80\x9d of the offices which have many valuable records pertaining to a number of cases.



'

