By then, cops had already started blocking off the area with guard rails but locals were still in the dark about the reason behind the intensified policing. An hour later, the drama intensified when a team of officers from the anti-rowdy squad of Kolkata Police and Shakespeare Sarani police station reached the area and whisked the CBI officials to the police station. The road was shut within 30 minutes as chief minister Mamata Banerjee reached the CPs residence. Later, she held a press conference right in front of the house as residents and passersby stopped to listen, and click selfies and shoot videos. 

\xe2\x80\x9cI have never seen something like this happen near our home. This is one of the most peaceful localities in the city. The one other time we saw such confusion here was when a woman shot at some men on Short Street six years ago,\xe2\x80\x9d said Anjali Jaiswal who lives a few blocks away from the CP\xe2\x80\x99s house. She had brought her son to see what was going on. 

Labourers at an under-construction high-rise opposite Kumar\xe2\x80\x99s residence were seen craning their necks to see over the gates and walls to record what was happening on their cellphones. Some motorists even stopped their cars and bikes and mingled among the journalists, watching the drama unfold. 

\xe2\x80\x9cI was passing by the area when I learnt about the incident and heard that the CM was going to address a press conference here. This is the first time I have seen the CM up close, so I made sure to take a few selfies and recorded the press conference. I have already sent the video to some friends on WhatsApp,\xe2\x80\x9d said Tollygunge resident Pankaj Shaw. 

